== Deals with the Devil ==
A Devil Room has a high chance of spawning [[item]]s that will be put up for sale. Unlike {{r|Shop}}s, where Isaac pays with money, to make Deals with the Devil Isaac has to trade Red [[Heart Container]]s as payment. All items normally cost either 1 or 2 Red Heart Containers, and their prices roughly correspond to their power.

When playing as {{C|Keeper}}, the character's [[Health#Coin Hearts|coin heart containers]] are used to trade for Devil Deal items, with items costing the same number of coin heart containers as red heart containers with a different character.

* {{Dlc|r}} Instead of coin heart containers, Devil Deal items must be bought using coins. One-heart and two-heart deals cost 15 and 30 cents, respectively. Paying cents for Devil Deals will still remove the Angel room appearance chance in the same way when other characters pay with heart containers.
** The same cost for deals are applied with any character who collected {{i|A Pound of Flesh}}.

''See the {{ip|Devil Room|text=Devil Room item pool}} for a comprehensive list of items offered and their health price.'' 

{{dlc|r+}} Additionally, Devil Deal items with the [[Item Tags devilsacrifice|<code>devilsacrifice</code> item tag]] will have a sacrifice spike cost instead of a Red [[Heart container|Heart Container]] cost. There is a 50% chance to award the item on the first play and 100% chance on the second. Picking up an item from the pedestal spawned this way counts as taking a regular deal and will prevent Angel Rooms from spawning naturally.

=== Notes ===
* If Isaac does not have Red Heart Containers upon entering a Devil Room, all items will cost 3 {{e|Soul Heart}}s.
** {{dlc|a}} If Isaac is presented with 2+ items to buy, but only has enough Red Hearts to buy one, the price of the other(s) will change to 3 Soul Hearts upon spending your Red Hearts.
** {{dlc|r}} Additionally, if Isaac only has one Red Heart, deals that normally cost 2 Hearts will change to one Red Heart and two Soul Hearts.
*** If Isaac does not have enough Soul Hearts for this type, he will still be able to take the Deal. However, if Isaac has no health at all (e. g. he is defying death with {{i|Berserk!}}), he will not be able to take the Deals.
** {{dlc+|a+nr}} If Isaac has less than 3 Soul Hearts, but at least one {{e|Bone Heart}}, he can take a three-Soul-Heart Deal and stay alive because of the bone hearts.{{dlc-}}
*** {{dlc|r}} Bone hearts are considered Heart Containers. Having at least one bone heart will change the price of a Deal to at least one red heart.
* Two-heart deals can be taken even if Isaac does not have enough Red Hearts to afford them, as long as he has one Red Heart to spend.
* Spending all of his Heart Containers will not kill Isaac as long as he has {{e|Soul Heart}}s, {{e|Black Heart}}s, or {{e|Bone Heart|nr}}s remaining.
** If taking a Deal leaves Isaac with no health remaining, he can still survive if he picks up a Soul Heart, Black Heart, or Bone Heart while holding the item in the air. Also, if he has an active item that grants Soul/Black Hearts, he can take a Deal and then use the active item, leaving him alive with whatever the item gave him.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EEdBTgyKxqU</ref> The same is true for consumables that give hearts (e. g. {{p|Dagaz}}).
*** {{dlc+|a}} If Isaac takes a Deal for an item that grants an {{e|Eternal Heart}} through the use of {{I|Chaos}}, it will ''not'' keep him alive.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|nr}} The temporary heart container granted by {{p|XI - Strength}} cannot be used to purchase a devil deal. However, if Isaac has no other heart containers to spend, then it can be used this way. This also works if the devil deal costs 2 hearts, but Isaac only has 0 or 1 before activating the Strength card.
** {{dlc|r}} Temporary heart containers can be used for devil deals with no restrictions.
* {{dlc|r}} Some items may cost Soul Hearts even if Isaac still has Red Hearts.
** An item's price may change from Red Hearts to Soul Hearts if Isaac visits the Devil Room before obtaining enough Soul Hearts and returning to the Devil Room.

=== Angel Rooms ===
* Refusing to make Deals with the Devil will give Isaac the chance of an {{r|Angel Room}} replacing the {{r|Devil Room}} on subsequent floors. If any Deal with the Devil is taken, Angel Rooms will not spawn for the remainder of the run.
** {{dlc|nr}} Trading Heart Containers for items in a {{r|Black Market}} counts as taking a Deal with the Devil for {{R|Angel Room}} generation purposes.
* Only the act of paying health (Red Hearts or Soul Hearts) for an item in a Devil Room counts as a Deal with the Devil. Taking {{e|Black Heart}}s, opening {{e|Red Chest}}s, and taking items that weren't paid for (such as those obtained from {{e|Red Chest}}s, {{e|Krampus}}, {{m|Beggar}}s, {{i|Pandora's Box}}, or made free by using {{p|Credit Card}}) do not count as Deals taken, allowing Isaac to still see Angel Rooms.
* {{dlc|r}} If the first offered Devil Room is not entered at all, the next offer is guaranteed to be an Angel Room. If the player uses the {{P|Joker}} it will take you to the Angel Room without removing the guarantee.

== Conditions to Make Devil Rooms Appear ==
A {{r|Devil Room}} can only open on floors between the second floor of [[Chapter 1]] and [[Chapter 4]].

There is only a 1% base chance for the Devil Room door to open. This chance can be modified in various ways:
